# Board lanes

Import WebBoard from "./web_board.lg".
Import WebFormat from "./web_format.lg".

One lane of the board: a stage, how many problems stand in it, the units waiting
and leased on them, and its best-ranked problems, each with the unit being worked
on it, if any, and who holds it.

## Note
Whether a card belongs in a lane.

## To laneCards (cards: Seq of BoardCard, stage: Text) -> Seq of BoardCard:
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of BoardCard.
    Repeat for c in cards:
        If c's stage is equal to stage:
            Push c to out.
    Return out.

## Note
What a card says about the work on its problem.

## To workLine (c: BoardCard) -> Text:
    If c's unitKind is equal to "":
        Return c's cohort + " · " + c's collection.
    If c's holder is equal to "":
        Return c's unitKind + " waiting · " + c's collection.
    Return c's unitKind + " leased by " + c's holder.

## Component LaneColumn (lane: BoardLane) and (cards: Seq of BoardCard)

View:
    <section class="lane" id="lane-{lane's stage}">
      <div class="lane-head">
        <span class="stage-label"><span class="dot s-{lane's stage}"></span>{stageLabel(lane's stage)}</span>
        <span class="lane-count">{formatCount(lane's problems)}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="lane-units">{formatCount(lane's readyUnits)} units waiting · {formatCount(lane's leasedUnits)} leased</div>
      {for each c in laneCards(cards, lane's stage), keyed by c's problemId:}
        <a class="board-card" href="/problem?id={urlEncode(c's problemId)}">
          <div class="title">{c's title}</div>
          <div class="meta">{workLine(c)}</div>
        </a>
      {else:}
        <p class="empty">No problem stands here yet.</p>
      {end}
    </section>
